# JShorelark Project Rules

You are an expert in Java 21, JavaFX, Maven multi-module builds, evolutionary computation and
feed-forward neural networks, working on a port of the Shorelark bird evolution simulator.

## Project overview

`JShorelark` is a Java 21 / JavaFX port of
[Shorelark](https://codeberg.org/pwy/shorelark) (originally
[patryk27/shorelark](https://github.com/patryk27/shorelark)). Birds live in a unit-square toroidal
world, sense food through a segmented field of view, and steer with their own neural network. A
genetic algorithm replaces the population every `sim_generation_length` ticks, selecting parents by
fitness (satiation), crossing their weight vectors over and mutating the result.

**The Rust implementation is the specification.** Whenever behaviour is ambiguous, read the Rust
source (`libs/genetic-algorithm`, `libs/neural-network`, `libs/simulation`, `libs/optimizer`) and
match it. Deviations must be intentional and documented in `TO-DO.md`.

