## Modules

| Module | Role | May depend on |
|---|---|---|
| `config-resources` | Checkstyle / PMD / Log4j2 resources shared by every module | nothing |
| `genetic-algorithm` | Chromosome, selection, crossover, mutation, statistics | JDK, Jackson annotations |
| `neural-network` | Layer, Neuron, NeuralNetwork, topology, weight (de)serialisation | `genetic-algorithm` |
| `simulation` | Config, World, Bird, BirdEye, BirdBrain, Food, Simulation | `genetic-algorithm`, `neural-network` |
| `optimizer` | PicoCLI commands, parallel grid search, JSONL logs, CSV analysis | `simulation` |
| `simulation-ui` | JavaFX application, Canvas renderer, controls, charts, sound | `simulation` |

Rules that keep the boundaries honest:

1. The three domain modules are **pure Java**: no `javafx.*`, no `java.io` file APIs, no
   `System.out`, no threads.
2. `simulation-ui` observes `Simulation`; it never mutates birds directly to "fix" what the domain
   should be doing.
3. `optimizer` owns the only `System.out` and `Files` usage outside JavaFX.
4. `config-resources` is a resource jar; it must not gain Java sources.

