## Build facts

- Root aggregator: `io.jshorelark:jshorelark-parent:1.0-SNAPSHOT`, `packaging=pom`.
- Java release is a property (`java.version`, currently `21`) referenced by `maven.compiler.release`.
- All dependency versions are properties in the root POM; module POMs never repeat them.
- Spotless, Checkstyle, SpotBugs, PMD and JaCoCo are configured in `<pluginManagement>` and opted
  into per module, except the gates that must run everywhere.
- `config-resources` is a dependency of every module that needs Checkstyle/PMD resources; when a
  quality configuration must change, change it there and let the modules pick it up.

Useful commands (from the repo root):

```bash
mvn -B -ntp spotless:apply
mvn -B -ntp -DskipTests package
mvn -B -ntp test
mvn -B -ntp verify
mvn -B -ntp -pl simulation-ui javafx:run
mvn -B -ntp -pl optimizer exec:java -Dexec.args="simulate -o results.jsonl"
```

## Coding conventions beyond the style guide

- Records for value types (statistics, log entries, configuration snapshots). Lombok `@Value` /
  `@Builder` / `@With` only where a record cannot express the shape (Jackson builders, mutable
  simulation objects).
- `@RecordBuilder` for records that need a Jackson-friendly builder or a fluent `with…` API.
- Getters follow record style (`position()`, `speed()`) in new domain records; existing Lombok
  `getX()` accessors stay until the surrounding code is modernised in one coherent change.
- Naming: `Bird` not `Animal`; `BirdEye` / `BirdBrain` mirror the Rust `Eye` / `Brain` split.
- No static mutable state anywhere. Constants are `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` and `static final`.
- Logging via `@Slf4j`, parameterised (`log.debug("… {}", value)`), never string concatenation. The
  domain logs sparingly; adapters log process detail.
- User-visible strings live in the UI layer. When adding text, keep it ready for externalisation
  (no string concatenation that cannot be translated).

## Testing expectations

- JUnit 6 (`junit-jupiter`) + AssertJ; Mockito only for adapter seams.
- Domain tests must be deterministic: pass a `new Random(seed)` instead of relying on the global
  random source.
- Port Rust tests that encode behaviour (eye vision grids, neuron propagation, GA golden output,
  statistics median for even/odd sizes).
- Coverage gate: 80% lines for the domain modules; UI and CLI are exercised by a small smoke test
  instead of pixel assertions.

